;;; A region claim that lists a fact of a relation only a rule's `:assert` derives
;;; is refused —
;;; M1f **W78**, register row `W78/solve-claim-derived-relation`, filed by S1f.7.11 (T1f.7.11.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `claim-derived-relation.ein` with its claim about the state: `(solve … :expect
;;; (region (model (admitted Ann) (paid Ann))))`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; R is root's state alone, and of `admitted` and `paid`, the relations the claim
;;; names, it holds `(admitted Ann)` and `(paid Ann)`: the claim holds, exit 0.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `73a0c17d`, release: refused at load, *(solve … :expect …) names admitted, which
;;; no declaration or fact makes a relation*, exit 1 on every command.
;;; A claim's relation is a relation of the program since S1f.7.11 (T1f.7.11.3):
;;; the claim loads and holds.

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(rule welcome ()
  :match  (paid ?g)
  :assert (admitted ?g)
  :why "{?g} has paid, so {?g} is admitted")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(solve :hypothesis-relations ()
       :expect (region (model (admitted Ann) (paid Ann))))
